Enterprise AI Underwriter Platform — Full Stack (v6.1)

Description:
This repository contains the complete enterprise-grade AI underwriting platform, including:

1. Policy LLM Service (Code Set 3) – High-throughput inference engine with SLOs, saturation monitoring, and automated remediation.


2. Next-Gen PII Deletion API + Worker (Code Set 4) – Async, transactional PII deletion with auditing, DLQ, Vault secrets, and Prometheus observability.


3. AI Underwriter API Service (Code Set 5) – Enterprise ingestion API, local/remote LLM risk scoring, idempotency, S3 uploads, PDF validation, and full observability.



The stack is designed for high reliability, observability, and compliance with enterprise data protection and audit standards.


---

Architecture Overview

Client/API
    │
    ▼
FastAPI Ingestion API (Code Set 5)
    │
    ├─ Auth (API Key / JWT)
    ├─ Idempotency (Redis)
    ├─ PDF Malware Checks
    ├─ Background S3 Uploads
    ├─ Metadata Enqueue (Redis Stream)
    │
    ▼
Policy LLM Service (Code Set 3)
    │
    ├─ Local LLM Model or Remote API
    ├─ SLO & Latency Monitoring (Prometheus)
    ├─ GPU/Queue Saturation Metrics
    ├─ Automated Remediation (Autoscaling / Region Failover / Security Mitigation)
    │
    ▼
PII Deletion Worker (Code Set 4)
    │
    ├─ Async queue consumer
    ├─ Transactional deletion + audit logging
    ├─ DLQ with retry_count metrics
    ├─ Optional Fernet encryption
    ├─ Prometheus metrics
    │
    ▼
Observability & Monitoring
    │
    ├─ Prometheus (metrics for LLM, API, worker)
    ├─ Grafana dashboards (SLO, queue growth, GPU utilization)
    ├─ Structured logging + audit trails
    ├─ Sentry (API exceptions)


---

Components

1. Policy LLM Service (Code Set 3)

Purpose: High-throughput model inference with automated alerting and remediation.

Key Features:

Prometheus SLO recordings:

TPOT P95 latency

HTTP error rates (5m fast, 1h slow)

GPU utilization and queue growth metrics


Alerts:

LLMTokenGenerationSlowdown → scale inference workers

LLMErrorBudgetBurningFast/Slow → region failover

LLMSaturationDetected → warn on queue growth

SecurityAgentHighRiskSignal → trigger security mitigation


Automated Remediation:

Vertical Pod Autoscaling

Traffic failover to another region

WAF rate limiting & certificate rotation


Grafana Dashboards:

TPOT P95, error budget burn, queue growth




---

2. Next-Gen PII Deletion API + Worker (Code Set 4)

Purpose: Ensure secure, auditable deletion of PII data with async, transactional reliability.

Key Features:

FastAPI enqueue endpoint with JWT authentication

Idempotent inserts using unique constraints in DB

Async worker:

Processes PII records in transactional batches

Generates chained SHA256 audit hashes

Updates processed flags and retries with backoff

Moves failed jobs to DLQ after max retries


Vault integration with retry to load DB & JWT secrets

Prometheus metrics:

Enqueue counts, worker success/failure, retries, DLQ count, latency


Health endpoint (/health)

Graceful shutdown of worker tasks


Database Tables:

1. pii_records — queued PII deletion tasks


2. deletion_audit — hashed audit trail


3. pii_dlq — failed deletion records




---

3. AI Underwriter API (Code Set 5)

Purpose: Enterprise ingestion API for insurance applicants, risk scoring using LLM, and secure storage of PII.

Key Features:

Endpoint: POST /apply

Accepts applicant data + optional PDF documents

Performs malware checks on PDFs

Calls local or remote LLM for risk assessment

Stores metadata and encrypted PII in Redis stream

Returns risk score and internal_id for tracking


Security:

API Key (X-API-Key) and JWT verification

Optional Fernet encryption for PII


Idempotency:

Uses X-Idempotency-Key + Redis TTL


Background file uploads to S3 with retry and DLQ

Circuit breaker for LLM calls

Prometheus metrics:

HTTP requests, latency, queue length, LLM calls, S3 uploads, idempotent skips


Sentry integration for exceptions

Logging & audit with correlation IDs and PII-safe masking



---

Configuration

Environment Variables (example)

Variable	Purpose

APP_NAME	Application name
ENV	Environment (prod/test)
INGESTION_API_KEY	API key for ingestion
JWT_SECRET	Optional JWT secret
REDIS_URL	Redis connection
S3_BUCKET	S3 bucket for document storage
S3_REGION	S3 region
S3_MAX_FILE_SIZE	Max upload file size
LOCAL_LLM_MODEL	Local LLM model for scoring
LLM_API_BASE_URL	Remote LLM API endpoint
PROMETHEUS_METRICS_PORT	Metrics port for API/Worker/LLM
ENCRYPTION_KEY_FOR_PII	Optional Fernet key for encryption
VAULT_URL	Vault server URL for secrets
VAULT_TOKEN	Vault token


Other tuning variables exist for rate limiting, retries, worker count, GPU scaling, etc.


---

Observability

Prometheus metrics for all components (LLM, API, Worker)

Grafana dashboards:

LLM SLOs, token latency, GPU utilization, queue growth


Structured logs with correlation IDs and PII-safe masking

Sentry for API exception monitoring



---

Deployment

Prerequisites:

Redis cluster

S3 bucket

Optional Vault server

Kubernetes / Docker environment recommended


Steps (simplified):

# Clone repo and set environment
git clone <repo-url>
cd <repo>

# Environment setup
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with secrets, API keys, S3, Redis, Vault info

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run API service (includes ingestion, LLM client, metrics)
uvicorn api.src.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

# Run PII deletion worker (if separate deployment)
python pii_worker.py

# Policy LLM service with PrometheusRule configs (Code Set 3) deployed via Kubernetes
kubectl apply -f policy-llm-rules.yaml
kubectl apply -f policy-llm-alerts.yaml

Scaling:

LLM inference can scale horizontally with automated remediation

Redis stream handles multiple workers for ingestion and deletion

Prometheus metrics allow alert-based autoscaling



---

Security & Compliance

Enforces JWT + API key access

Optional PII encryption with Fernet

PDF malware scans

Audit trails with deterministic hashes

DLQ ensures retries and visibility into failed deletions

Alerting for LLM saturation, token latency, error budget burn, security signals



